WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
- So, and actually, Seth Rogen
produces the show, right?

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.090
So did you have to audition for him?

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:05.072
Was that nerve wracking?

00:00:05.072 --> 00:00:05.905
- I did.

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.690
It was, he is a,

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.640
you guys picked the most
intimidating picture

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.182
I've ever seen of Seth Rogen.

00:00:11.182 --> 00:00:13.730
(laughing)

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:15.942
He's like, audition for me please.

00:00:15.942 --> 00:00:18.070
- Oh my God, you sounded like him.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.150
- [Female] Yeah, that was good.

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.604
- I do my best.

00:00:20.604 --> 00:00:21.870
No, I had to audition for him,

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:23.950
which was super nerve wracking
'cause he's one of my heroes,

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:25.951
him and his writing
partner, Evan Goldberg,

00:00:25.951 --> 00:00:28.240
and I remember I was
pacing in the hallway,

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:30.180
going over my lines and
he hadn't showed up yet,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.108
and then like seemingly a
mile away I could hear like,

00:00:33.108 --> 00:00:33.941
(vocalizes laughter)

00:00:33.941 --> 00:00:36.180
I could hear his iconic laugh

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.550
and I was like, oh he's here.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.645
And then once we got into the room,

00:00:39.645 --> 00:00:44.520
it was insane because he was
reading Butcher on the day.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.630
Butcher is a character
in the show who has a

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:49.080
very thick, Cockney accent

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.800
so it was Seth Rogen not doing the accent,

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.540
but saying lines that involved a lot of

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.330
hardcore Cockney slang,

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:59.720
which my brain was really
struggling to understand,

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.240
you know, what reality I was in.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.870
It would be like, I would
say a line and he would say,

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.050
we got to get them in the boot

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:06.810
and then we're going to bugger off.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.397
It was really-

00:01:08.397 --> 00:01:09.952
(laughing)

00:01:09.952 --> 00:01:11.460
- Is he trying to throw you off your game?

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.810
Is this what it was, like?

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.210
- I don't think so.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.680
He's a very, very nice guy.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:18.311
It was just one of those
moments where I was so nervous

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:22.287
and I was just, I was so crazy.

00:01:22.287 --> 00:01:25.110
No, I don't think he would
intentionally do that,

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:26.450
but memorable to say the least.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:27.990
- He seems like somebody
that might mess with someone.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:30.853
That's the only reason why I'm saying it.

